Optimal Solution - Compare the original array with its sorted version and count index mismatches.
                   “I clone the array, sort it, and count how many indices differ from the original.”

class Solution {
    public int heightChecker(int[] heights) {
        int n = heights.length;   // Length of array
        int count = 0;            // Counts mismatched positions
        int expected[] = new int[n];  // Copy of original array
        // Copy elements into expected array
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            expected[i] = heights[i];
        }
        // Sort the copied array
        Arrays.sort(expected);
        // Compare original and sorted arrays
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (heights[i] != expected[i]) {
                count++;          // Increment if mismatch found
            }
        }
        return count;  // Return total mismatches
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(n log n).
Space Complexity :- O(n).
